  "cover_text": "Headed over to the O.co Coliseum for the Oakland Athletics’ 2020 season opener, the squad put together a 7-0 record for their start to their new home. Though one of the more questionable defenders from the A’s, Bryce Harper has totally transformed since he came to Oakland, and Drew Patterson is seeing a useful season starting off at 1-1.\nTaking a look over the first half of the season, the Yankees were put on track to be the league’s best club offense. But because of second baseman Yadier Molina’s struggles with injury, the team suffered their third consecutive first half loss to the Marlins at Yankee Stadium.\nDamnation Me",
